{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: take the three salvageable pieces out of the closed README head 6ef29521 as their own small change. Filed as its own request because the authorization those hunks currently stand on, 51da7efc, is retired and world-stale, so nothing may inherit it. This request is their new basis.\n\nTHE ONE THAT MATTERS. You found that README.md is not gated by the documentation set at all: DocsDir is \"docs\", the walker never reaches the repository root, and so nothing checks that the most-read file in the project has links that resolve or examples that run. Close that. TestREADMERelativeLinksResolve from the dormant head is a starting point, not a specification -- you verified its eleven links still resolve and its example still runs clean against a gs built from current main, exit 0. Decide whether the right shape is extending the docset walker to cover the repository root or a targeted test, and say why.\n\nTHE TWO SMALL ONES, which you reported auto-merge clean. The docs/why.md three-hunk de-overclaim: every document becomes many documents, documents-name-the-acts becomes tracked-artifacts-name-the-acts with the re-check-not-wrong gloss, and the paragraph stating that gitseq does not discover causal edges from files, imports or prose. And the matching one-hunk change in docs/README.md.\n\nWHAT NOT TO BRING. Nothing else from that head. Not the README rewrite, not the jq demo, and above all not TestREADMELeadsWithTheTrackedArtifactOutcome, which I rejected in 381c031a for pinning prose byte for byte on a file that changes constantly.","body":{"area":"docs","conditions":"README.md is covered by a gate that fails when a relative link in it does not resolve, and that gate must be reached by the ordinary make test path rather than run by hand. State in the artifact whether you extended the documentation walker to the repository root or added a targeted test, and why that shape is right; if the walker now covers the root, say what else newly falls under it and confirm nothing that was previously ungated is now red. Apply the docs/why.md and docs/README.md de-overclaim hunks from 6ef29521 as ordinary edits on current main, not as a merge or rebase of that head, which is closed and whose authorization is retired. Do not pin prose byte for byte and do not introduce a banned-phrase list. Prove the new gate fails when a README link is broken and passes when it is fixed, and prove that mutation rather than asserting it. Run gofmt, go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 and the documentation gate with -count=1 at the exact head. Publish exact-head artifacts for every changed stable path and request an independent review with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.","severity":"low","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}